---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import AffiliateShowcase from '../components/AffiliateShowcase.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sri Yantra Vastu & Placement Guide — Directions, Home Temple & Puja"
  description="Vastu Shastra rules for placing Sri Yantra in home: North-East (Ishan Kon) alignment, facing East or North, Friday activation rituals, and dos & don'ts."
  canonicalPath="/vastu/"
  isDark={false}
>
  <Header isDark={false} />

  <main class="article-page">
    <article class="article-container">
      <header class="article-header">
        <div class="category-tag">Vastu Shastra & Sacred Placement</div>
        <h1 class="display-title article-title">
          Where to Place Sri Yantra in Your Home: The Complete Vastu & Worship Guide
        </h1>
        <p class="article-subtitle">
          Essential Vastu Shastra rules for direction, orientation, Friday Prana Pratishtha activation, and answering common questions on maintaining sacred geometry at home.
        </p>

        <div class="author-meta">
          <span>By <strong>Atharva Mahamuni</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/athmatwt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@athmatwt</a>)</span>
          <span class="meta-dot">•</span>
          <span>9 Min Read</span>
          <span class="meta-dot">•</span>
          <span>Vastu Guidelines</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="article-content">
        <p class="lead-paragraph">
          The <strong>Sri Yantra (Shri / Shree Yantra)</strong> is considered the premier energetic catalyst in Vastu Shastra. Because it radiates cosmic bio-energy and attracts prosperity, its placement within your home or office space dictates the flow of positive vibrations.
        </p>

        <h2>1. The Best Location in the House</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Pooja Room (Home Temple):</strong> The most sacred and ideal location. Place the yantra on the main altar resting on a clean red or yellow silk cloth.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Study or Workstation:</strong> Placing a small copper or crystal Sri Yantra on your work desk enhances mental clarity, focus, and productivity.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Near Cash Box or Financial Locker:</strong> In Vastu, keeping a consecrated Sri Yantra near your safe or financial accounts attracts stability and clears financial blockages (ensure the safe opens facing North).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Living Room Showcase:</strong> A 3D Maha Meru pyramid placed in a clean, elevated cabinet in the North-East zone brings domestic harmony.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Exact Vastu Direction & Orientation</h2>
        <div class="highlight-callout">
          <div class="callout-title">The Golden Direction: North-East (Ishan Kon)</div>
          <p>
            The <strong>North-East (*Ishan Kon*)</strong> is the supreme direction for placing the Sri Yantra. This zone is ruled by divine spiritual energy and clarity. Alternatively, the <strong>East</strong> (direction of the rising sun) is also highly favorable.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h3>Which Direction Should the Yantra Face?</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>The Yantra itself should face towards the <strong>East</strong> or <strong>North</strong>.</li>
          <li>When you sit to pray, meditate, or chant before the Sri Yantra, you should ideally be <strong>facing East or North</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Directions to Avoid:</strong> Never position the Sri Yantra facing South, as this interferes with the subtle pranic current.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Frequently Asked Vastu Questions</h2>
        
        <h3>Can we keep Sri Yantra at home?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes, absolutely. Keeping a Sri Yantra at home is highly auspicious. While elaborate temple-level Tantric rites (*Navavarna Puja*) require initiation, keeping a 2D copper plate or 3D crystal Sri Yantra at home with daily cleanliness and reverence brings peace and clears negative Vastu doshas.
        </p>

        <h3>Can we keep two Sri Yantras at home?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes. You may keep more than one Sri Yantra provided they are kept in separate, respectful areas—for example, one on your Pooja altar for spiritual worship, and a small copper or crystal one on your office study desk for mental concentration.
        </p>

        <h2>4. How to Activate (Prana Pratishtha) at Home</h2>
        <ol class="activation-steps">
          <li><strong>Auspicious Day:</strong> Perform installation on a Friday morning during Shukla Paksha (waxing moon) or on a Purnima (full moon).</li>
          <li><strong>Purification:</strong> Gently wash the yantra with raw milk and holy Gangajal, then dry it with a pristine, soft cloth.</li>
          <li><strong>Altar Setup:</strong> Spread a fresh red or yellow silk cloth in the North-East corner of your altar. Place the Yantra facing East.</li>
          <li><strong>Light Offerings:</strong> Light a pure cow ghee diya (oil lamp) and fragrant sandalwood incense.</li>
          <li><strong>Chanting:</strong> Chant the sacred seed mantra <em>"Om Shreem Hreem Kleem Shreem Namah"</em> or <em>"Om Aim Hreem Shreem Sri Matre Namah"</em> 108 times using a Lotus seed (*Kamal Gatta*) or Sphatik mala.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>5. Vital Vastu Rules & Precautions</h2>
        <div class="rules-box">
          <div class="rule-item negative">
            <span class="rule-icon">✕</span>
            <span>Never place the Sri Yantra directly on the bare floor; always elevate it on an altar or wooden stand.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="rule-item negative">
            <span class="rule-icon">✕</span>
            <span>Avoid placing sacred yantras inside bedrooms directly under or near beds.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="rule-item positive">
            <span class="rule-icon">✓</span>
            <span>Keep the surrounding area dust-free, pristine, and clutter-free.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="rule-item positive">
            <span class="rule-icon">✓</span>
            <span>Treat the Sri Yantra with sincere reverence rather than treating it merely as passive decorative art.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <!-- Verified Sourcing Cards -->
  <AffiliateShowcase />

  <Footer isDark={false} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .article-page {
    padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem 5rem;
    background-color: var(--color-canvas);
  }

  .article-container {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .article-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .category-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .article-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .article-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    color: var(--color-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .author-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }

  .meta-dot {
    color: var(--color-hairline-strong);
  }

  .article-content {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .lead-paragraph {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .article-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 2.75rem 0 1rem;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .article-content h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .article-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-body);
  }

  .article-content ul, .article-content ol {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-body);
  }

  .article-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .highlight-callout {
    background-color: var(--color-primary-soft);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .callout-title {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .activation-steps {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .rules-box {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
  }

  .rule-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .rule-item.negative {
    background-color: rgba(207, 45, 86, 0.08);
    color: #cf2d56;
  }

  .rule-item.positive {
    background-color: rgba(31, 138, 101, 0.08);
    color: #1f8a65;
  }

  .rule-icon {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }
</style>
